From: scalpel4k <scalpel4k@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btqca: declare QCC2072 firmware

btqca builds its firmware names at runtime and declares none. Image
builders (dracut, image-janitor fw-cleanup in the openSUSE Agama installer)
rely on MODULE_FIRMWARE and drop qca/ornbtfw*.tlv, ornnv*.bin and
ornbcscal*.bin, so the QCC2072 falls back to ROM firmware.

Upstream candidate (would need all supported chips).
---
diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
@@ -1125,3 +1125,7 @@
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Ben Young Tae Kim <ytkim@qca.qualcomm.com>");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Bluetooth support for Qualcomm Atheros family");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
+/* QCC2072 ("orn"): patch, NVM and calibration files, any ROM version */
+MODULE_FIRMWARE("qca/ornbtfw*.tlv");
+MODULE_FIRMWARE("qca/ornnv*.bin");
+MODULE_FIRMWARE("qca/ornbcscal*.bin");
